      "tooltip": "A protected line (dhc:Circuit) — the unit the C-Box validates. Sits on a board rail. Its `line` variable is the token loads reference via 'protected by'. The `differential` variable references the dhc:RCD device protecting it — SHARED referencing is how the topology is expressed: all circuits → one differential = one-per-install (older NF C 15-100); one differential per rail = one-per-rail (newer editions). An RCBO circuit is its own differential (protection = RCBO). On blockly→abox it becomes dhc:Circuit + dhc:hasProtection (its breaker + the referenced RCD) + dhc:hasWiring.",
      "helpUrl": "",
      "data": "dhc:blocklyBlockTemplate=dhc:Circuit",
      "mutator": "dhc_points_mutator"
